# Everything in here is local working memory for coding-agent sessions.
#
# One file per working day, named for the date and for what that day actually
# did: YYYY-MM-DD-short-title.md. No generic README, no index — the newest
# filename should tell you what happened without opening it.
#
# Each file carries, in this order:
#   1. What changed      — grouped by concern. Name the bug, not the edit.
#   2. Why               — the reasoning not recoverable from the code.
#   3. Verified          — what was run, and its result. "10 files green", not
#                          "tests pass".
#   4. Found, not fixed  — noticed in passing. Highest value for a later session.
#   5. Next              — concrete, ordered, startable cold.
#
# Read the newest file before starting work, and verify any claim against the
# source before acting on it — these notes describe what was true when written.
#
# This folder is deliberately NOT part of the repository's history: it goes stale
# fast, it describes intent rather than code, and a reviewer reading the git log
# should see commits, not a diary. Ignore everything except this file, so the
# folder itself stays in the tree and a fresh clone still has somewhere to write.
*
!.gitignore
